OL,3,CDisgraced newsreader allowed to enter
OL,4,CEisteddfod poetry competition
OL,6,FHe also said he hoped readers would
OL,7,Ffind the piece "illuminating".
OL,9,FWriters entering the Eisteddfod's
OL,10,Fpoetry competition do so anonymously,
OL,11,Fwith their real identities kept in an
OL,12,Fenvelope and only revealed if they are
OL,13,Fannounced as the winner. Festival
OL,14,Forganisers said they would review the
OL,15,Fprocess - as they do every year.
OL,17,FThe National Eisteddfod said: "All
OL,18,Fcompetitors in our main literary
OL,19,Fcompetitions submit their entries
OL,20,Funder a nom de plume.
OL,1,Wj5hw}j5 ~shws                   G3/4
OL,2,W+.-'*%/"-$+,(,'T(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
